* Example 08: the NMOS sink array at the operating point the removed `emir
* layout` simulated (out at 1.8 V, vb at 1.0 V), every source held at DC over a
* short transient (EM's currents come from a .tran). run.sh writes
* tb_op_rcc.cir and tb_op_cc.cir from this file, as tb_tran.cir.in.
.param mc_mm_switch=0 mc_pr_switch=0
.include "@PDK_ROOT@/sky130A/libs.tech/ngspice/corners/tt.spice"
.include "@PDK_ROOT@/sky130A/libs.tech/ngspice/r+c/res_typical__cap_typical.spice"
.include "@NETLIST@"

Vout out 0 1.8
Vvss vss 0 0
Vvb vb 0 1.0
Xdut vb out vss sink
.options timeint reltol=1e-4
* (four 1 ns windows, a step no longer than 20 ps: the run's window is whole)
.tran 0.01n 4n 0 0.02n
.end
